{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement","id":1462005,"title":"What Roles Do You Think The Tzimisce Fill In The Anarch Movement?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-29T13:57:20-07:00","id":1462005,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What Roles Do You Think The Tzimisce Fill In The Anarch Movement?","content":"The V5 Companion states that there is a divide between the Old Tzimisce who have redoubled the claims on their ancient homelands and the Young Tzimisce who have flocked to the Anarch Movement and that few hate the Elders as much as a Tzimisce. Although there has been much said about the activities of the Brujah, Gangrel and more recently Ministry participation in the Movement, I'm sure I'm not the only one frustrated at the lack of Anarch praxis, politics and factions being fleshed out in the books. With that said, how do you think the Tzimisce participate in the &quot;new&quot; Anarch Movement? What roles would they take? What skills and experience do you think the Movement will benefit from?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:06:19-07:00","id":1462008,"title":"","content":"Hypothetical Scenario (Totally not based on one of my games*):<br /> <br /> <b>A Tzimisce joins the Anarchs</b><br /> <br /> Lief, Brujah: So, you're Tzimisce, right?<br /> <br /> Zard, Tzimisce: Shim-A-Shay, yes.<br /> <br /> Lief: So, welcome to the Anarchs. I think you'll find it very different from the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Zard: This is my address. *hands business card*<br /> <br /> Lief: What?<br /> <br /> Zard: It is a two-story mansion with an extensive basement that I will be expanded. Do not enter this property upon pain of death. In exchange, I will proceed to offer to alter any and all of your gang's facial features. I can make them blindingly beautiful, different from their mortal identities, or grotesque but I understand most aren't into that.<br /> <br /> Lief: You can't just...what?<br /> <br /> Zard: I will participate in your meetings and also any and all attempts to assassinate Elders or Ancilla of the Camarilla or Sabbat. I will engage in diablerie or not as befitting agreed upon terms ahead of time regarding war spoils. Furthermore, I will not feed on any mortals you personally list but require the feeding on the UCLA Mathematics Department be left to me. Do we have an accord?<br /> <br /> Lief: Uh, sure I guess.<br /> <br /> Zard I find this equitable. Here is a potted plant to symbolize our new status as allies, fellow Anarch.<br /> <br /> Lief: It's bleeding.<br /> <br /> Zard: You're welcome.<br /> <br /> * It's totally based on one of my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-29-2021, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:14:09-07:00","id":1462010,"title":"","content":"They don't. Tzmisce are terrifying, evil and alien. I think that's how they actually 'work' since they're a natural conflict point. I've had the idea of playing one of them in v5 coming to terms with her re-emerged humanity after years in the Sabbat as her concience catches up with her","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:22:54-07:00","id":1462012,"title":"","content":"For a more serious answer:<br /> <br /> Tzimisce who join the Anarchs are almost certainly doing so because they view it as a more viable alternative to the Camarilla but the Sabbat has become unpalatable. I'm inclined to think the defectors are those who think they're all being used as cannon fodder in the Gehenna War, the Antediluvians cannot be defeated, or they have gotten themselves free of the Vinculum. Maybe those rare Low Humanity/Non Path Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Generally, I think those Tzimisce who will join the Anarchs are going to be aloof from the sect as a whole. They will be part of the Anarchs and give it their sect-based allegiance but you aren't going to find many die-hard idealogues. I wouldn't be surprised if there were Tzimisce Barons but these guys are going to rule their districts autocratically even by Camarilla standards and be &quot;Anarchs&quot; only in the sense they're against the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if quite a few of these Tzimisce would still be on Paths of Enlightenment but do the best to keep their more humane cohorts from knowing JUST how fucked up and evil they are. They'd still have a reputation probably as murderers and cold-blooded monsters but HOW bad they are would be something they might restrict to their basements, dungeons, storage facilities, and secret laboratories.<br /> <br /> Basically, I imagine the defecting Tzimisce are going to be Sabbat-lite and fulfill the serial kiler description of, &quot;Seemed like a nice man, very polite, kept to himself.&quot; They will be joining the Anarchs for security and not to be conscripts in a hopeless suicidal war. Their childer are going to be perhaps more likely to be on the Path of Humanity but I suspect either Low Humanity or Blood Bonded/Dominated out the wazoo despite their new sect.<br /> <br /> I could see the Tzimisce also providing &quot;unpleasant but necessary&quot; services as Cleaners for the vampires of the area like body-disposal, assassinating those mortals who need to be taken care of, and perhaps also disappearing Anarchs who are unwilling to get with the program. If you accept the Sabbat among you, you probably expect them to do the dirty-work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:23:31-07:00","id":1462013,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">I don't see a lot they are geared to contribute. Any sort of spiritual mysticism or arcane knowledge is either redundant with the Ministry and Ipsissimus Tremere, or worse, rendered completely inert with V5 changes. With their new Dominate acquisition, they might have an easier time accumulating quick money, but they will hoard it for themselves and maybe even try to steal your own shit if the compulsion grabs them just right.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">What they can get <i>from</i> the Movement is probably more important to them, which would be a level of &quot;fuck the Elders&quot; freedom, or at least an acceptable illusion of that.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:28:31-07:00","id":1462015,"title":"","content":"To me the principle role of the Tzimisce that they bring to the Anarchs is that of Warlord. Like for all the high minded ideals of egalitarianism that some Anarchs profess, a whole lot are mostly just the club for vampires that want a bigger piece of the pie. Tzimisce aren't really interested in being part of a bigger organization that they can manipulate like the Lasombra are, they want to generally be able to be left alone to run their stuff how they want it to be run. So there's no general incentive for Sabbat defectors to join the Camarilla like the Lasombra had, but the Tzimisce do like the idea of having some form of allies that they can go to if they need help in things in exchange for minimal interference.<br /> <br /> So yeah a lot of Anarch Tzimisce are going to stake out their bit of territory, pledge allegiance to the Anarch cause, but they're not really interested in playing revolutionary politics of even thinking that much about any other vampires if they have to. A lot of Anarchs are going to be somewhat put off by the Tzimisce who just looks like he's running his own little fiefdom within their domains, they'll question his sincerity to the cause, and whether he's truly interested in any radical change in power dynamics.<br /> <br /> But when the Camarilla has decided they've had enough and try to assert themselves in town, or Sabbat resurge in power or the SI Hunters cracks down, the Tzimisce will be there faithfully fulfilling his obligations to the cause, a pack of his flesh-warped horror ghouls right behind him. And what happens next won't be pretty, but it will be damn efficient, and once they're done they'll consolidate their gains, leave the rest of the Anarchs to worry about the optics, and settle back down to their private pursuits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T14:36:54-07:00","id":1462016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462015#post1462015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the principle role of the Tzimisce that they bring to the Anarchs is that of Warlord. Like for all the high minded ideals of egalitarianism that some Anarchs profess, a whole lot are mostly just the club for vampires that want a bigger piece of the pie. Tzimisce aren't really interested in being part of a bigger organization that they can manipulate like the Lasombra are, they want to generally be able to be left alone to run their stuff how they want it to be run. So there's no general incentive for Sabbat defectors to join the Camarilla like the Lasombra had, but the Tzimisce do like the idea of having some form of allies that they can go to if they need help in things in exchange for minimal interference.<br /> <br /> So yeah a lot of Anarch Tzimisce are going to stake out their bit of territory, pledge allegiance to the Anarch cause, but they're not really interested in playing revolutionary politics of even thinking that much about any other vampires if they have to. A lot of Anarchs are going to be somewhat put off by the Tzimisce who just looks like he's running his own little fiefdom within their domains, they'll question his sincerity to the cause, and whether he's truly interested in any radical change in power dynamics.<br /> <br /> But when the Camarilla has decided they've had enough and try to assert themselves in town, or Sabbat resurge in power or the SI Hunters cracks down, the Tzimisce will be there faithfully fulfilling his obligations to the cause, a pack of his flesh-warped horror ghouls right behind him. And what happens next won't be pretty, but it will be damn efficient, and once they're done they'll consolidate their gains, leave the rest of the Anarchs to worry about the optics, and settle back down to their private pursuits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br /> <br /> One thing ANARCHS UNBOUND mentioned was the irony that many Anarch domains are either very egalitarian (in the sense that if they dislike the leader, they will rip him apart) or the leader has more power than any Prince could dream of because he has no Primogen or Elders but himself as People's Leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T15:31:44-07:00","id":1462025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462016#post1462016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with this.<br /> <br /> One thing ANARCHS UNBOUND mentioned was the irony that many Anarch domains are either very egalitarian (in the sense that if they dislike the leader, they will rip him apart) or the leader has more power than any Prince could dream of because he has no Primogen or Elders but himself as People's Leader.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I disagree with the idea that they wouldn't be interested in revolutionary politics as they were pretty much the spearhead of the original Anarch Revolt. Like the book said, nobody hates an Elder as much as a Tzimisce does and I would think they would be all in on rolling out the guillotines. In fact,since they helped kick the whole thing off, I could see the Tzimisce as considering themselves the &quot;owners&quot; of the Movement and being very invested in its success.<br /> <br /> Then you have quotes like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To hear the hoariest tales, some Voivode lords have themselves become one with their havens, or even suffused themselves into their homelands, merging their consciousness with the very soil of the domain. What better way to show ownership of the land and its folk than to become that very land and sustain the generations to come? </div> </div> </div>Which shows how protective a Tzimisce can be over the places and people it considers its own. Imagine a few of these defending a free state and its people? With their covetous compulsion interpreted as a want to recruit people to the Movement and expand its territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s not a gang so much as it is a way to make sure everyone\u2019s watching everyone else\u2019s back when the rest of the world has written them off. The Gang Leader goes out of the way to show how everyone working toward a common goal that society tells them they can\u2019t have simply needs to reach out and take it </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possessed not of a traditional land domain, the Special Forces Commandant has instead the nigh\u0002fanatical respect of their unit, and their soldiers would follow them into Hell itself. So the Special Forces Commandant bides their time and trains their troops, for when they can perhaps parlay an insurrection or policing action into a greater claim of domain. </div> </div> </div>These are from the Tzimisce Archetypes. And when you think about the Vaulderie, which was started by the original Anarch Tzimisce, I think they could really excel in the role as Movement commissars and captains training and leading them in war or defending their territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:38:20-07:00","id":1462042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462025#post1462025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I disagree with the idea that they wouldn't be interested in revolutionary politics as they were pretty much the spearhead of the original Anarch Revolt. Like the book said, nobody hates an Elder as much as a Tzimisce does and I would think they would be all in on rolling out the guillotines. In fact,since they helped kick the whole thing off, I could see the Tzimisce as considering themselves the &quot;owners&quot; of the Movement and being very invested in its success.<br /> ...<br /> Which shows how protective a Tzimisce can be over the places and people it considers its own. Imagine a few of these defending a free state and its people? With their covetous compulsion interpreted as a want to recruit people to the Movement and expand its territory.<br /> ...<br /> These are from the Tzimisce Archetypes. And when you think about the Vaulderie, which was started by the original Anarch Tzimisce, I think they could really excel in the role as Movement commissars and captains training and leading them in war or defending their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I think the Tzimsce are very interested in taking down Elders and the like, but I think with them you're running into different questions of the forms of freedom the Anarchs are after. I think that whether they're an elder or a neonate, the average Tzimisce is going to have a difficulty not treating those around them as their possessions, it's their compulsion to do so. Possessions may be treated well, but there's still an undeniable hierarchy at play that's not at all dissimilar to the elder dominant society. So in that regard the revolt is less a rejection of that society, and more a sense that many Tzimisce neonates felt like they were in the wrong place, especially with elders messing with their things. Sort of a &quot;freedom for me, not for thee&quot; kind of idea<br /> <br /> So yeah, this does mean that Anarch Tzimisce aren't likely to be disloyal to the cause, but they're not going to really care about the opinions of the other vampires that make up that cause. And while they're going to be very interested in taking down elders and tearing down the power structures that they see as limiting and oppressing, in any subsequent anarch domain the best case result is they keep their own domain and leave the rest of the Anarchs to their own ideals so long as they're left alone, or they institute themselves as Baron and create an even worse regime than the one they tore down. (Which yes, could involve reintroducing Vaulderie to ensure collective loyalty)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T17:32:42-07:00","id":1462049,"title":"","content":"Warlords, witches, scholars, tacticians, rule enforcers, spies, financial backers, philosophers, march wardens/border guards, and secret police are just the ones that occur off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T19:08:10-07:00","id":1462059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462042#post1462042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I think the Tzimsce are very interested in taking down Elders and the like, but I think with them you're running into different questions of the forms of freedom the Anarchs are after. I think that whether they're an elder or a neonate, the average Tzimisce is going to have a difficulty not treating those around them as their possessions, it's their compulsion to do so. Possessions may be treated well, but there's still an undeniable hierarchy at play that's not at all dissimilar to the elder dominant society. So in that regard the revolt is less a rejection of that society, and more a sense that many Tzimisce neonates felt like they were in the wrong place, especially with elders messing with their things. Sort of a &quot;freedom for me, not for thee&quot; kind of idea<br /> <br /> So yeah, this does mean that Anarch Tzimisce aren't likely to be disloyal to the cause, but they're not going to really care about the opinions of the other vampires that make up that cause. And while they're going to be very interested in taking down elders and tearing down the power structures that they see as limiting and oppressing, in any subsequent anarch domain the best case result is they keep their own domain and leave the rest of the Anarchs to their own ideals so long as they're left alone, or they institute themselves as Baron and create an even worse regime than the one they tore down. (Which yes, could involve reintroducing Vaulderie to ensure collective loyalty)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I think &quot;possession&quot; can be stretched in a lot of directions and can mean every different things to different people. It can be possessive in a caretaker sense, to a friendship sense (they are MY friends) to nothing more than tools to exploit. Like I said before, I think it's possible that the Tzimisce could view themselves as &quot;owning&quot; the Anarch Movement since they were the ones that started it and therefore owning its ideals as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T19:37:30-07:00","id":1462065,"title":"","content":"The crazy shut-in, or recluse, that most everyone avoids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:01:26-07:00","id":1462082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462065#post1462065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The crazy shut-in, or recluse, that most everyone avoids.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Tzimisce anarchs are just like your average tabletop role-players? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:18:56-07:00","id":1462089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462082#post1462082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Tzimisce anarchs are just like your average tabletop role-players? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like we need more Embraced gamers.<br /> <br /> I feel like they should be a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T23:20:08-07:00","id":1462090,"title":"","content":"Ironically the Tzimisce have always had a hand in the movement, although idk I would describe their roll. The Tzimisce have always valued personal pursuits over politics, and the Anarchs do kinda represent this. In fact, when the movement started in the late Dark Ages, it was the Tzimisce that began work to further take power from the elders. Yes this ended up creating a whole new sect, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T00:47:33-07:00","id":1462099,"title":"","content":"I think they are able to leverage a lot of influence, especially if they bring on some other Sabbat defectors. Beyond their powers, the fact that young Tzimisce are particularly hateful of elders probably makes them the ones trying to revitalized the Anarchs back to their state during the First Anarch Revolt. They also have a lot of stuff useful for gangs and the like with Vicissitude and Dominate, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T01:27:25-07:00","id":1462104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462008#post1462008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Zard I find this equitable. Here is a potted plant to symbolize our new status as allies, fellow Anarch.<br /> <br /> Lief: It's bleeding.<br /> <br /> Zard: You're welcome.<br /> <br /> * It's totally based on one of my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cackled. <br /> <br /> <br /> In seriousness. I think the Tzmisce would join the Anarchs purely out of Dislike for the Sabbat and Camarilla, but in a more defensive than offensive role, or at least they'd encourage others to do the abroad fighting for them. Tzmisce are really more of a support/service based clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T09:02:33-07:00","id":1462135,"title":"","content":"Joking aside, I always had some issues with the proscriptive nature of the old World of Darkness. Such as there supposedly being no Lasombra, Tzimisce or Giovanni among the Anarchs. I can easily see Lasombra and Tzimisce defecting to the Anarchs for a number of reasons, and Giovanni among the rabble as spies. In any case, what individual Tzimisce are doing with the Anarchs will vary to much to easily generalize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T11:34:32-07:00","id":1462142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462135#post1462135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joking aside, I always had some issues with the proscriptive nature of the old World of Darkness. Such as there supposedly being no Lasombra, Tzimisce or Giovanni among the Anarchs. I can easily see Lasombra and Tzimisce defecting to the Anarchs for a number of reasons, and Giovanni among the rabble as spies. In any case, what individual Tzimisce are doing with the Anarchs will vary to much to easily generalize.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean technically speaking one of the most powerful Anarchs in America is a Lasombra, Marcus Vitel, Emperor of Washington DC. How reasonably one can actually call him an Anarch is debatable since he's mostly just the guy in charge who's not interested in being under the Camarilla's thumb. (And when the guy's a two thousand year old Methuselah that already survived your previous assassination attempt, there's not a lot of good counter arguments). But other Anarch Barons are willing to work with the guy, so the affiliation isn't worthless.<br /> <br /> I agree though that I like that V5 is at least moving in the direction towards letting clan and sect affiliation be more free from, even if there are still official Camarilla or Anarch clans, I tend to emphasize that there's very little stopping an individual kindred from being part of whatever sect they want. The Camarilla's certainly more exclusive, but to some extent things like the Lasombra invitation are more just about there being a standard precedent for how they can join, whereas if a Tzimisce wanted to join the Camarilla there's probably going to be even more hoops or special exceptions necessary to get them through the door. With the Anarchs its more just going to be about whether the local Anarchs are willing to acknowledge you as being an ally rather than any clear-cut procedures. If a Lasombra comes along saying he wants in, they may think he's a spy, or ask for a loyalty test, or they may be hard stretched enough that they can't afford to be choosers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T14:43:43-07:00","id":1462164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462142#post1462142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean technically speaking one of the most powerful Anarchs in America is a Lasombra, Marcus Vitel, Emperor of Washington DC. How reasonably one can actually call him an Anarch is debatable since he's mostly just the guy in charge who's not interested in being under the Camarilla's thumb. (And when the guy's a two thousand year old Methuselah that already survived your previous assassination attempt, there's not a lot of good counter arguments). But other Anarch Barons are willing to work with the guy, so the affiliation isn't worthless.<br /> ers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Classic case of &quot;my enemy's enemy is my friend.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind you, I actually like the idea that most Anarchs aren't angry at the Camarilla because it is oppressive but they're not the oppressors. Like the Ferengi.<br /> <br /> Marcus just had to give money and domain to gain the loyalty of Baltimore's Anarchs and make them his army.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T16:35:20-07:00","id":1462172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462142#post1462142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree though that I like that V5 is at least moving in the direction towards letting clan and sect affiliation be more free from</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a profoundly weird impression, because it was pretty free form before Revised, far more than now.<br /> <br /> No rule, even unwritten, stopped anyone from becoming a member of the Camarilla, no matter clan or bloodline. The &quot;Official clans&quot; are just the ones with enough of a presence for the average Kindred to know them and expect their presence in a city, secondarily with a member in the Inner Council and a Justicar for whatever that was worth.<br /> <br /> But the Lasombra were already a sizable presence in the Cam and none of the sects had any problem accepting any particular clan. Well, with the exception of the Baali.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T16:52:07-07:00","id":1462175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462172#post1462172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a profoundly weird impression, because it was pretty free form before Revised, far more than now.<br /> <br /> No rule, even unwritten, stopped anyone from becoming a member of the Camarilla, no matter clan or bloodline. The &quot;Official clans&quot; are just the ones with enough of a presence for the average Kindred to know them and expect their presence in a city, secondarily with a member in the Inner Council and a Justicar for whatever that was worth.<br /> <br /> But the Lasombra were already a sizable presence in the Cam and none of the sects had any problem accepting any particular clan. Well, with the exception of the Baali.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Promise specifically forbids the Giovanni from holding any position in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> But you are otherwise correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T18:13:45-07:00","id":1462195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462025#post1462025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you have quotes like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To hear the hoariest tales, some Voivode lords have themselves become one with their havens, or even suffused themselves into their homelands, merging their consciousness with the very soil of the domain. What better way to show ownership of the land and its folk than to become that very land and sustain the generations to come? </div> </div> </div>Which shows how protective a Tzimisce can be over the places and people it considers its own. Imagine a few of these defending a free state and its people? With their covetous compulsion interpreted as a want to recruit people to the Movement and expand its territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine most Tzimisce who identify THAT strongly with their lands never left Eastern Europe in the first place. But I do see ones that held on to their clan culture through their time in the Sabbat finding the feudal setup the Anarchs operate under attractive and familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T19:59:47-07:00","id":1462204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462172#post1462172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a profoundly weird impression, because it was pretty free form before Revised, far more than now.<br /> <br /> No rule, even unwritten, stopped anyone from becoming a member of the Camarilla, no matter clan or bloodline. The &quot;Official clans&quot; are just the ones with enough of a presence for the average Kindred to know them and expect their presence in a city, secondarily with a member in the Inner Council and a Justicar for whatever that was worth.<br /> <br /> But the Lasombra were already a sizable presence in the Cam and none of the sects had any problem accepting any particular clan. Well, with the exception of the Baali.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not the impression I got. Like isn't the key mystery of DC by night the fact that Vitel is actually a Lasombra pretending to be a Ventrue, with the distinct implication that if the truth was known they would assume that Vitel was working with the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Like I'm sure there were Lasombra defectors before 5e, but I still got a distinct impression that there was an assumption that if a vampire was from a traditionally Sabbat clan it would be a very weird exception if they weren't part of the Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T20:16:39-07:00","id":1462206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462204#post1462204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the impression I got. Like isn't the key mystery of DC by night the fact that Vitel is actually a Lasombra pretending to be a Ventrue, with the distinct implication that if the truth was known they would assume that Vitel was working with the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Like I'm sure there were Lasombra defectors before 5e, but I still got a distinct impression that there was an assumption that if a vampire was from a traditionally Sabbat clan it would be a very weird exception if they weren't part of the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it was found out that Vitel was a Lasombra, the Camarilla IMMEDIATELY took a hit out on him.<br /> <br /> Mind you, sending Theo Bell and Christof may have been intended to get them killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:07:50-07:00","id":1462218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462204#post1462204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the impression I got. Like isn't the key mystery of DC by night the fact that Vitel is actually a Lasombra pretending to be a Ventrue, with the distinct implication that if the truth was known they would assume that Vitel was working with the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Like I'm sure there were Lasombra defectors before 5e, but I still got a distinct impression that there was an assumption that if a vampire was from a traditionally Sabbat clan it would be a very weird exception if they weren't part of the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitel faked his clan and identity, conspired against the previous Prince, used the Ventrue clan structure to plot her destruction and became one of the most powerful and well-connected members of the sect while impersonating. What would you expect to happen if they find they were duped? This has little to do with him being Lasombra and everything to do with him impersonating a Ventrue to the clan's higher-ups.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra <i>antitribu</i> were frequent enough to be called out by that name, they're not considered common, but are common enough to be a known thing. And the sects, again, had exactly zero rules against clan participation except the Giovanni Promise. The Camarilla expected every kindred to follow its laws and, as long as they were, extended its protection. The Anarchs accepted anyone that wanted to bring down the powers that be. And the Sabbat indoctrinates without care about clan as long as you followed the ritae and proved your loyalty to the sect.<br /> <br /> Only in <i>Revised</i> the clan divide became really more strict. Before that a Tzimisce in the Cam would certainly, surely receive a lot of weird expressions, but it would be feasible and absolutely in the spirit of the sects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:26:01-07:00","id":1462219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462218#post1462218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitel faked his clan and identity, conspired against the previous Prince, used the Ventrue clan structure to plot her destruction and became one of the most powerful and well-connected members of the sect while impersonating. What would you expect to happen if they find they were duped? This has little to do with him being Lasombra and everything to do with him impersonating a Ventrue to the clan's higher-ups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but if his clan wasn't a big deal to begin with, why did he go out of his way to pretend to be a Ventrue for literal decades in the first place? Like he actually had a unique magic item that negated his clan bane so he would cast a reflection, that's a lot of work if you could have just gone &quot;Yup, I'm Antitribu, grr, hate me those Sabbat guys.&quot; and people would have been just fine with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:37:49-07:00","id":1462222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462219#post1462219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay but if his clan wasn't a big deal to begin with, why did he go out of his way to pretend to be a Ventrue for literal decades in the first place? Like he actually had a unique magic item that negated his clan bane so he would cast a reflection, that's a lot of work if you could have just gone &quot;Yup, I'm Antitribu, grr, hate me those Sabbat guys.&quot; and people would have been just fine with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- The item is useful, period.<br /> 2- He had, in fact, been a member of the Sabbat centuries before, so he wanted to throw <i>his own identity off</i>, regardless. Faking clan makes it easier.<br /> 3- Also he wanted the political power of the Ventrue, specifically.<br /> <br /> Vitel joined the Sabbat almost at the beginning, but merely for seeing it as an opportunity to fulfill his political ambitions. Seeing that the true power was with the Camarilla and he had joined the losers (to his specific standards), he abandoned it and went to the New World to get lost for a time and rebuild anew in the future. He went torpid in the area before DC even existed, and figured he had awaken in what was arguably the most powerful city in the world.<br /> <br /> He specifically wanted to be the Prince of DC, no matter what, because ultimate power gave him the giggles. So he went for the impersonation more likely to give him just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:39:01-07:00","id":1462223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462219#post1462219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay but if his clan wasn't a big deal to begin with, why did he go out of his way to pretend to be a Ventrue for literal decades in the first place? Like he actually had a unique magic item that negated his clan bane so he would cast a reflection, that's a lot of work if you could have just gone &quot;Yup, I'm Antitribu, grr, hate me those Sabbat guys.&quot; and people would have been just fine with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the implication I got is that being a Lasombra is in fact a horrifyingly dangerous thing and he'd never have been trusted with the Princedom of America's capital.<br /> <br /> Camarilla?<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> Actual power? No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T21:53:31-07:00","id":1462224,"title":"","content":"Important note: Guide to the Camarilla not only pointed out that the Lasombra <i>Antitribu</i> were a thing as it also squarely stated that Tzimisce <i>Antitribu</i> weren't, but the reasoning behind it tells a lot about the sect question.<br /> <br /> The book states that it will be surprising if the Tzimisce in the Cam are half a dozen, insufficient to call that an <i>antitribu</i>, and they're probably in the sect just for a temporary goal and then go independent.<br /> <br /> Although it outright meant that there was no plans on making canonical Cam Tzimisce characters, that also meant:<br /> - Lasombra in the Cam were a sizable enough presence;<br /> - Tzimisce in the Cam existed;<br /> - It was not that hard to enter, otherwise such temporary memberships wouldn't be possible;<br /> - Probably isn't 100%, so any exception would still be valid in lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T22:11:32-07:00","id":1462228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462224#post1462224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important note: Guide to the Camarilla not only pointed out that the Lasombra <i>Antitribu</i> were a thing as it also squarely stated that Tzimisce <i>Antitribu</i> weren't, but the reasoning behind it tells a lot about the sect question.<br /> <br /> The book states that it will be surprising if the Tzimisce in the Cam are half a dozen, insufficient to call that an <i>antitribu</i>, and they're probably in the sect just for a temporary goal and then go independent.<br /> <br /> Although it outright meant that there was no plans on making canonical Cam Tzimisce characters, that also meant:<br /> - Lasombra in the Cam were a sizable enough presence;<br /> - Tzimisce in the Cam existed;<br /> - It was not that hard to enter, otherwise such temporary memberships wouldn't be possible;<br /> - Probably isn't 100%, so any exception would still be valid in lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Lasombra Revised book gave some insights into the Lasombra Antitribu and said they were a thing.<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition was much more, &quot;They don't exist and we hunt them everywhere they're found.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think a huge chunk of the Antitribu's popularity also came from the introduction of Lucita before they decided to make her a stereotypical Lasombra because the Signature character shouldn't be unique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T01:25:53-07:00","id":1462250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1462228#post1462228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a huge chunk of the Antitribu's popularity also came from the introduction of Lucita before they decided to make her a stereotypical Lasombra because the Signature character shouldn't be unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure Lucita was taken by a C:tL's True Fae and that thing is a fetch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T15:41:17-07:00","id":1463481,"title":"","content":"So I was looking up some Tzimisce in the lore to confirm my view of how they can fit into the Anarchs and i think I found some:<br /> <br /> Daliah who was a a Sabbat blood doll turned Anarch from Miami.<br /> <br /> Dr. Vermundo de Sancha who is extremely protective of his patients who he considers under his protection and fully abides by the hippocratic oath.<br /> <br /> Ilyana Dmitju hunter of nazis and skinheads and protector of Roma people.<br /> <br /> Ratti-Ben revolutionary and champion of the downtrodden and lower caste people of India.<br /> <br /> Zachary Sikorsky a non-binary person who was an active part of the New York queer community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T22:15:43-07:00","id":1463542,"title":"","content":"I like how everyone's answer to how a Tzimisce would fit into the Anarchs was to perpetuate existing archetypes - in effect trying to cram the Tzimisce as they've always been portrayed into a new sect - rather than asking why a Tzimisce being <i>different</i> might lean them towards the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> I understand that it might just be me, a perennial Soft Boi who just wants people to get along, but when I thought of why a Tzimisce might join the Anarchs, my mind leapt to &quot;because they're less evil and more social, and want a sect that rewards that&quot;. If not actually being high Humanity, then <i>wanting</i> to be. Or otherwise not having the retiring personality typical of Tzimisce, and actually wanting to mingle.<br /> <br /> There are doubtless tons of Cainites embraced into the Sabbat for whom little could be more unbearable or personally repulsive. The Sabbat embrace scores of vampires just as cannon fodder. Over a long enough time frame, some of the ones for whom the Sabbat ethos is a poor fit will manage to survive their initial suicide mission. And, rather than being broken by all the systemic attempts to make them conform to Sabbat attitudes, only grow more convinced that the sect sucks and they should leave. Whether they end up being stuck there, suffering in silence, until their Vinculum chances to be broken on its own, or whether they duck out early enough that they can resist its effects, they get out and look for any alternative.<br /> <br /> Since the Camarilla is the Camarilla, with all that this implies, many such Cainites might end up going to the Anarchs by default. It provides freedom, the attempts at egalitarianism, a resistance to Elder control, and no expectation that you go around committing atrocities for any or no reason.<br /> <br /> Are the Anarchs the ideal sect for this? No. Do they always live up to their lofty goals? Hell no. But it's a much better fit any most every other sect.<br /> <br /> <br /> An Anarch Tzimisce is the most likely of any of their Clan to break with convention about being reclusive serial killers and amoral scientists/artists of flesh. Which leaves room for exploring what a flesh-crafting vampire would be like if you DON'T assume from the outset they must be evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T11:51:52-07:00","id":1463603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462005-what-roles-do-you-think-the-tzimisce-fill-in-the-anarch-movement?p=1463542#post1463542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how everyone's answer to how a Tzimisce would fit into the Anarchs was to perpetuate existing archetypes - in effect trying to cram the Tzimisce as they've always been portrayed into a new sect - rather than asking why a Tzimisce being <i>different</i> might lean them towards the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> I understand that it might just be me, a perennial Soft Boi who just wants people to get along, but when I thought of why a Tzimisce might join the Anarchs, my mind leapt to &quot;because they're less evil and more social, and want a sect that rewards that&quot;. If not actually being high Humanity, then <i>wanting</i> to be. Or otherwise not having the retiring personality typical of Tzimisce, and actually wanting to mingle.<br /> <br /> There are doubtless tons of Cainites embraced into the Sabbat for whom little could be more unbearable or personally repulsive. The Sabbat embrace scores of vampires just as cannon fodder. Over a long enough time frame, some of the ones for whom the Sabbat ethos is a poor fit will manage to survive their initial suicide mission. And, rather than being broken by all the systemic attempts to make them conform to Sabbat attitudes, only grow more convinced that the sect sucks and they should leave. Whether they end up being stuck there, suffering in silence, until their Vinculum chances to be broken on its own, or whether they duck out early enough that they can resist its effects, they get out and look for any alternative.<br /> <br /> Since the Camarilla is the Camarilla, with all that this implies, many such Cainites might end up going to the Anarchs by default. It provides freedom, the attempts at egalitarianism, a resistance to Elder control, and no expectation that you go around committing atrocities for any or no reason.<br /> <br /> Are the Anarchs the ideal sect for this? No. Do they always live up to their lofty goals? Hell no. But it's a much better fit any most every other sect.<br /> <br /> <br /> An Anarch Tzimisce is the most likely of any of their Clan to break with convention about being reclusive serial killers and amoral scientists/artists of flesh. Which leaves room for exploring what a flesh-crafting vampire would be like if you DON'T assume from the outset they must be evil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. I think of all the clans the Tzimisce are the most pigeon holed by players. That's why I've tried to show examples of characters in the lore that don't quite conform to the stereotype while also still being part of the clan archetype.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I have a question for anybody who can answer. What do people think of the Children of the Dracon being some of the Tzimisce that came over to the Anarchs post the Sabbat collapse? I know they are cool with Thin Bloods and are the ones to disobey the Elders the most. Also, since they follow the Dream of Constantinoble, they might have common cause with the Anarch dream of Carthage? But to clarify my knowlage of Constantinople is woefully lacking so I have no idea if that works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}